    "explanation": "Explanation: In NH3, the orbital dipole due to the lone pair points in the same direction as the resultant dipole of the three N-H bonds (reinforcing each other), resulting in a high dipole moment. In NF3, the orbital dipole points in the opposite direction to the resultant dipole of the three N-F bonds (opposing each other), resulting in a low dipole moment.",
